// B1 (2026-09-27): an effect performed INSIDE a spawned branch. The branch
// runs in the world it was spawned in — the task record carries the live
// install chain, the fresh instance installs it before the closure runs —
// so `op()` in each branch walks to `h`, installed at the fanout's own
// frame OUTSIDE the schedule. The race rule admits it: h is stateless
// (`resume(7)` writes no state record), so two instances resuming into it
// share nothing. Before this landing the branch started at world 0 and the
// first perform faulted at the 0x100000000 belt. Expected exit: 14.
effect E { op() -> Int }
handler h { op() => resume(7) }
fn main() = match (0 <| ({ _ => op() }, { _ => op() })) ~> parallel_compose ~> h {
  (a, b) => a + b,
}
